alt-syscall: allow rseq, clone3, faccessat2, close_range, pidfd_open and openat2 in "complete"

A current glibc, dbus and bubblewrap call all six on every process start or
on common paths (rseq registration at startup, clone3 for
posix_spawn/pthread_create, faccessat2 for access()/test -x, close_range in
exec helpers, pidfd_open in dbus-daemon and at-spi-bus-launcher to watch
their children, openat2 in bwrap to resolve mount destinations without
following symlinks). Under the enforcing "complete" table each one hit
block_syscall(), which returns -ENOSYS; userspace falls back, so nothing
broke, but every process start logged
"blocked syscall 334/434/435/436/437/439" and flooded dmesg.

The entries go in the section shared by all architectures: the table is
keyed on __NR_<name>, and all six exist on both x86_64 (334, 434, 435,
436, 437, 439) and arm64 (asm-generic: 293, 434, 435, 436, 437, 439), so
this covers both. The compat (32-bit) whitelist is unchanged.
